The receipts under receipts/ quote public metadata of two Hugging Face repositories,
both published under Apache-2.0: the file list, config.json and tensor names of
incoai/GLM-5.3-Flash-DFlash2 and of J-sandler/Qwen3-4B-DNeo. This project includes
no weights of either.

receipts/2026-11-20-pilot names the public Hugging Face datasets whose text the
pilot recording's prompts were made from, each with its revision and licence:
globis-university/aozorabunko-clean, HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2,
HuggingFaceFW/fineweb, llm-jp/magpie-sft-v1.0,
llm-jp/scaling-data-constrained-llms, nvidia/OpenCodeInstruct,
nvidia/Nemotron-Post-Training-Dataset-v1, nvidia/Nemotron-SWE-v1 and
OpenAssistant/oasst2. This project includes none of their text, and none of the
target's replies to oasst2's prompts.

open_dneo/drafter.py implements the two drafters' forward passes. It was written
to compute what these public definitions compute, and its tests compare it with
their outputs. No file of theirs is copied here:

- z-lab/dflash, dflash/model.py, at 07ebd93db9f472af339b644bb70221ad8428328a.
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Z Lab. DFlash2's layer, entrance, attention
  mask and candidate selector.
- J-sandler/Qwen3-4B-DNeo (Hugging Face), configuration_dneo.py, modeling_dneo.py
  and reference.py, at 8451a2e8446c0bfa09be47623ff044d896540ec4, and J-sandler/DNeo,
  src/dneo/runtime/dneo.py, at 8449a3ce891f6b3321efafc1e5c0c7e5c40e11c7.
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 sgl-project. DNeo's router, attention mask and
  folded head.
- Hugging Face Transformers, the Qwen3 modules those definitions build on (the
  norm, the MLP, the rotary embedding). Apache License 2.0.

tests/fixtures/ holds numbers those definitions computed with random parameters
at a small size; tools/reference/ holds the scripts that ran them and how to
fetch the definitions.

These modules read what TensorFold writes, or compute what it computes. They were
written from its source and documents at
e3fb56cb09061a979cb02080601fc6f7870d3362. No file of TensorFold's is copied here:

- open_dneo/recording.py: the recorder's files, from
  zig/src/core/lanes/recorder.zig and docs/recipes/training-a-drafter.md.
- open_dneo/rounds.py: where a chain of DFlash2 drafts is cut, from draftBlock in
  zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig; the rounds a stream decoded alone takes,
  from plan and copyProposal in zig/src/core/lanes/windows.zig, the round in
  engine.zig, and the drafts asked in depth.zig and open.zig.
- open_dneo/copies.py: the lookup that proposes a copy of a stream's earlier
  tokens, from SuffixLookup in zig/src/core/lanes/proposer.zig. Three of its tests
  use the cases of that file's own tests.
- open_dneo/drafter.py: a draft's chance among its candidates, from select in
  zig/src/families/glm/dflash_select.zig.
- open_dneo/score.py: the block and the context serving's DFlash2 drafter holds
  at a round, and its scores in bfloat16, from zig/src/families/glm/dflash.zig
  and dflash_block.zig.
- open_dneo/served.py: a 4-bit linear's values, from tf_glm_quantize4 in
  zig/kernels/cuda/glm_quant.cu, and which of the drafter's linears hold them,
  from zig/src/families/glm/dflash_load.zig.
- open_dneo/weights.py: an MXFP8 projection's values, from
  zig/src/families/glm/cuda_mxfp8.zig, and an E4M3 code's, from
  zig/src/core/quant/fp8.zig.
- tools/oracle/open_dneo_oracle_test.zig: a test to be placed in TensorFold's
  tree, which runs its lane core (zig/src/core/lanes) with GLM's facts from
  zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig and cuda_copy_policy.zig.
  tests/fixtures/lane_core_rounds.jsonl holds the rounds it wrote.

